{
  "status": "verified native indexed ribbon/mesh prerequisite; Phase 3.1 tubular helices remain in progress",
  "owner": "Phase 3.1",
  "source_before": "7c704104c9649954a8d3944d8da1290a490dff10",
  "implementation": [
    "Ribbons and caller meshes bind native Uint32 index buffers and five-word indexed indirect arguments in beauty, transparency and shadow passes. Analytic impostors keep their existing indirect draws.",
    "One IndexFormat type replaces the acceleration-only index encoding and serves both raster and acceleration geometry. All call sites migrated without an obsolete alias.",
    "Removing manual WGSL index lookup reduces the ribbon layout from eight to seven vertex storage buffers, leaving room for live fitted-axis poses within baseline WebGPU limits.",
    "Persistent grow buffers own their binding usage; topology edits reuse native index allocations. No additional frame buffer or per-atom draw submission is introduced.",
    "The native mesh regression exposed a preexisting incomplete shared bind group. Static meshes now bind every required layout entry and explicitly bypass spline deformation before any recipe read; unused storage entries reuse the resident vertex allocation."
  ],
  "complexity": "O(vertices + indices) scene-edit upload; O(1) draw recording per representation. Geometry sampling, physical profiles, immutable coordinates and image quality are unchanged.",
